WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.980
Over the years, a considerable number of innocent
people had unknowingly wandered into SCP-3008.

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:11.090
Otherwise known as the Infinite Ikea, this
extra-dimensional space more than lived up

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:16.070
to its nickname, consisting of an Ikea store
with no known limit to its endless aisles

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:19.130
upon aisles of flatpack Swedish furniture.

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:23.820
But given the veritable labyrinth contained
beyond the seemingly ordinary automatic doors

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:29.880
of SCP-3008’s entrance, it was rare that
anyone making their way inside ever made it

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.820
back out alive.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:36.070
On top of that, there was little the Foundation
could do to ensure the safe return of anybody

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:40.480
unlucky enough to find themselves lost in
the Infinite Ikea.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:45.620
Once inside, navigating a way out was made
almost impossible given the scope of the spatially

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.300
anomalous store.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:50.129
And then, of course, there was the Staff.

00:00:50.129 --> 00:00:56.070
These tall, humanoid creatures roamed the
aisles of SCP-3008, sporting a lack of facial

00:00:56.070 --> 00:01:01.940
features, disproportionate bodies, and wearing
the typical uniform of an average Ikea worker.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:05.420
“I think it’s becoming a concern,” Researcher
Conley declared.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:10.550
“No, a problem, just how many people are
going missing in SCP-3008.”

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:12.580
“What else can we do?”

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:15.500
her colleague Researcher Kylan replied, shrugging
their shoulders.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.580
“We keep watch over the entrance, stop anyone
entering.”

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:24.229
“But ours isn’t the only entrance,”
Conley retorted; it was true, based on evidence

00:01:24.229 --> 00:01:28.259
gathered from some survivors that had made
it out of the Infinite Ikea, the entrance

00:01:28.259 --> 00:01:31.299
seemed to exist in multiple parallel universes.

00:01:31.299 --> 00:01:36.759
“Say we could figure out not just a way
navigate through SCP-3008 with better accuracy

00:01:36.759 --> 00:01:41.299
so people can make it back out, but what if-”
“What if we could use it?”

00:01:41.299 --> 00:01:43.310
Kylan jumped in, finishing the sentence.

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:47.659
“It could be like an interdimensional spaghetti
junction, a hub to access all sorts of other

00:01:47.659 --> 00:01:49.260
alternate universes!

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:52.110
We could send people through the entrance
in our universe, and they could make their

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:55.110
way through SCP-3008 and out into another.”

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:56.110
“Exactly!”

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:57.110
their fellow researcher smiled.

00:01:57.110 --> 00:01:59.079
“One problem, though,” they said.

00:01:59.079 --> 00:02:01.500
“What do we do about the Staff?”

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:05.750
The inhabitants of the Infinite Ikea were
undoubtedly an obstacle standing in the path

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:07.909
of Conley and Kylan’s idea.

00:02:07.909 --> 00:02:13.690
The faceless creatures were known to be docile
during the daytime cycle within SCP-3008,

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:17.550
only to turn violent and attack anyone present
when the lights dimmed.

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:20.230
“They’re part of the problem,” Conley
mused.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:22.610
“But what if they could be part of the solution?”

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:27.660
The SCP Foundation hadn’t had much chance
to examine a live instance of a Staff member

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:30.650
– known as SCP-3008-2s – up close.

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:36.300
As such, they had a limited understanding
of exactly what these creatures truly were

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:39.790
beyond the few they had witnessed chasing
survivors out of the entrance.

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:41.239
Were they intelligent?

00:02:41.239 --> 00:02:46.819
They were apparently able to speak, if only
uttering the phrase “The store is now closed,

00:02:46.819 --> 00:02:48.790
please exit the building”.

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:52.879
Did they have the capacity for independent
thought, free will and emotionality?

00:02:52.879 --> 00:02:58.099
There was only one way to find out, and so
Conley presented her plan to capture a member

00:02:58.099 --> 00:03:02.409
of SCP-3008’s Staff for closer examination…

00:03:02.409 --> 00:03:06.549
not knowing the bizarre chain of events that
would unfold as a result.

00:03:06.549 --> 00:03:12.269
Drawing it out was the easy part of the plan;
after all, the Foundation knew that SCP-3008-2s

00:03:12.269 --> 00:03:16.010
were able to react to the presence of human
beings within the Infinite Ikea.

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:21.230
So, Conley proposed sending in a single member
of D Class personnel, with a line of cable

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:26.290
attached to them, tethering them to just outside
the entrance of SCP-3008.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:31.320
They were like the bait on the end of an interdimensional
fishing line, and would hopefully catch the

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:33.569
attention of a Staff member and lure them
out.

00:03:33.569 --> 00:03:35.709
“What do we do once it’s out?”

00:03:35.709 --> 00:03:36.709
Kylan had mused.

00:03:36.709 --> 00:03:39.629
“I mean, we know so little about their biology.

00:03:39.629 --> 00:03:42.400
We could use knockout gas, but what if they
don’t breathe?

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.510
We could tranquilize it, but what if they
don’t have blood?”

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:51.180
It had been the one hitch in Conley’s plan,
although she had suggested they use pure force,

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:54.480
trapping the Staff member like a wild animal
before bringing it back.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:04:00.870
And sure enough, as an instance of SCP-3008-2
came racing out of the Infinite Ikea, hot

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:05.569
on the heels of the D Class, Foundation security
officers were able to swoop in and capture

00:04:05.569 --> 00:04:10.450
the creature, restraining it and bundling
it into a transport back to the site.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:14.819
However, upon receiving their captive Staff
member, Kylan and Conley were faced with a

00:04:14.819 --> 00:04:16.009
new problem.

00:04:16.009 --> 00:04:20.389
The creature seemed to be in its passive state,
it didn’t seem to be aggressive while away

00:04:20.389 --> 00:04:22.449
from SCP-3008.

00:04:22.449 --> 00:04:26.960
Kylan had posited their theory that the Staff’s
attack state was linked somehow to the day

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:34.280
and night cycles within the Infinite Ikea,
and now separated from that space, the SCP-3008-2

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:35.289
would remain docile.

00:04:35.289 --> 00:04:38.759
But the larger issue was communicating with
it.

00:04:38.759 --> 00:04:43.039
As patient as Conley tried to be with the
faceless, mouthless humanoid, it seemed to

00:04:43.039 --> 00:04:46.400
be totally unresponsive to verbal communication.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:51.650
Any question she or her colleague Kylan asked
the Staff member, it offered no response.

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:56.920
Dialing it back to more basic methods of communication,
it didn’t react when presented with symbols,

00:04:56.920 --> 00:05:01.410
unphased by letters or numbers, or even straightforward
pictograms.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:06.080
No matter what they tried, the Staff member
they had captured seemed not unwilling, but

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:07.560
unable to respond.

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:12.180
“There’s got to be something we haven’t
tried,” Conley urged, her frustration building

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:14.490
after a long day of trying to get through
to the creature.

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:17.780
“They’re capable of speech, we know that
from witness reports.”

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:19.470
“Maybe they’re a hive mind?”

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:22.170
Kylan mused, equally exhausted after their
efforts.

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:26.590
“What if it shares a consciousness with
the other Staff, like a drone in an ant colony?

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:28.479
Hey, that’s what we should name this one!”

00:05:28.479 --> 00:05:29.479
they added.

00:05:29.479 --> 00:05:30.479
“Dee for drone!”

00:05:30.479 --> 00:05:32.780
“Can we focus here, please?”

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:33.780
Researcher Conley snapped.

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:36.860
“It’s almost like we need some way of
enhancing it, granting it the right higher

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:40.000
brain functions, so it has the ability to
speak with us.”

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.050
“Hold up,” her colleague replied.

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:46.160
“You said we need a way to enhance it…
but what if we refined it?”

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:51.960
What Kylan was insinuating was obvious, albeit
a direct violation of the Foundation’s own

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:52.960
rules.

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:58.289
SCP-914, otherwise known as the Clockworks,
was an anomalous contraption of unknown origin.

00:05:58.289 --> 00:06:02.520
Two booths connected to the machine, one labeled
‘Input’ and the other ‘Output’, could

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:07.289
be used to disassemble, recreate, improve
or destroy an object that was placed within

00:06:07.289 --> 00:06:08.530
SCP-914.

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:14.030
Although, there was yet again another hurdle
Conley and Kylan would have to attempt jumping

00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:18.789
over: the Foundation had banned the use of
the Clockworks on biological organisms.

00:06:18.789 --> 00:06:23.669
The pair submitted a request to their Foundation
superiors for access to SCP-914 and permission

00:06:23.669 --> 00:06:25.229
to use it on Dee.

00:06:25.229 --> 00:06:29.039
Kylan hadn’t expected their suggestion to
be met with anything short of a resounding

00:06:29.039 --> 00:06:33.949
‘no’, and while determined, Conley couldn’t
help but find herself worrying about the possible,

00:06:33.949 --> 00:06:38.010
highly likely rejection, which made it all
the more surprising that their request was

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:42.860
not only granted, but the experiment approved
by the O5 Council themselves.

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:47.569
Clearly, the highest operational staff within
the Foundation had some keen interest in whether

00:06:47.569 --> 00:06:51.370
the Clockworks could refine an SCP-3008 Staff
member.

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:56.069
More likely, their interest was in what benefits
the experiment could potentially lead to.

00:06:56.069 --> 00:07:00.410
If the Foundation possessed a refined Staff
member, its own agent within the Infinite

00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:05.240
Ikea, the possibilities could be of great
advantage to the O5 Council.

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:12.120
They were less concerned with having an intermediary,
using Dee to communicate with the other SCP-3008-2s,

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:16.979
or negotiating the potential release of the
displaced innocent people lost in the Infinite

00:07:16.979 --> 00:07:17.979
Ikea.

00:07:17.979 --> 00:07:22.680
If refining Dee could mean the Council had
a way to safely reach other alternate universes

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:29.199
by traversing through SCP-3008, then that
bridge between worlds would be theirs to control…

00:07:29.199 --> 00:07:33.919
Of course, Kylan and Conley were more interested
in what refining Dee could tell them about

00:07:33.919 --> 00:07:37.000
the Staff and the nature of SCP-3008.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:41.220
Did instances of SCP-3008-2 have needs, or
wants?

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:43.520
Could they even possess the capacity to want
things?

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:48.210
Were they fulfilled with their lives as anomalous
Ikea workers, and how did they navigate the

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:49.900
maze of endless aisles?

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:52.250
“Imagine it,” Conley theorized.

00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:56.389
“If Dee can communicate with them for us,
we could open up trade with them.

00:07:56.389 --> 00:08:01.610
The canteen inside SCP-3008 endlessly refills
with food, just picture what that could mean

00:08:01.610 --> 00:08:06.340
if we work out a system of distributing that
resource out of the Ikea… it could change

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:07.340
the world!”

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:08.530
she exclaimed excitedly.

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:10.490
“Only one way to find out, right?”

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:11.750
Kylan replied.

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:17.900
They watched as Dee, their captive Staff member,
was nudged into the Input booth of SCP-914.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:22.340
Conley gave the research assistants a signal
to activate the Clockworks, hoping that refining

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:25.810
Dee would allow them to be capable of speech
and free thought.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:30.759
However, either through miscommunication – or
a secret order from above – one of the assistants

00:08:30.759 --> 00:08:33.339
had incorrectly calibrated SCP-914.

00:08:33.339 --> 00:08:38.260
It was meant to be set to ‘Fine’ which
would improve whatever was placed in the machine.

00:08:38.260 --> 00:08:42.660
But instead, the dial had been turned to ‘Very
Fine’ which improved the target item to

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:47.130
an even greater extent – often granting
it anomalous properties.

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:52.850
Before anyone even noticed the change, the
gears and gyros of SCP-914 clicked and whirred

00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:57.450
into life, making a raucous noise of moving
mechanical parts.

00:08:57.450 --> 00:09:02.470
Destroyed in the Input booth only to be reconstituted
into something altogether new in the Output

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:07.589
one opposite, Dee emerged from SCP-914 after
the process was complete.

00:09:07.589 --> 00:09:08.589
Superficially, the creature didn’t look
much different.

00:09:08.589 --> 00:09:11.990
Its clothing seemed to have experienced the
most noticeable change.

00:09:11.990 --> 00:09:16.270
Instead of being the usual yellow shirt and
blue trousers Ikea uniform worn by the rest

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:21.550
of the staff, Dee was now sporting the same
clothes, but the colors seemed to be shifting,

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:24.510
almost like the natural camouflage of a chameleon.

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:29.510
They were still faceless, their body still
incorrectly proportioned compared with a human,

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:31.750
and for the most part Dee seemed unchanged.

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:36.400
But before Kylan and Conley could move in
to take a closer look, before they were even

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:41.339
able to check if Dee could speak, the Staff
member vanished in the blink of an eye.

00:09:41.339 --> 00:09:45.589
An instant state of panic erupted throughout
the Foundation facility, alarms were howling

00:09:45.589 --> 00:09:49.800
over a containment breach, security teams
were dashing through every wing of the Site

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:51.490
to track down Dee.

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:56.120
Swept up in the chaos that quickly ensued,
Conley and Kylan received another message

00:09:56.120 --> 00:10:01.209
from the highest point up the chain of command:
find that Staff member and bring it in alive.

00:10:01.209 --> 00:10:05.160
Or there would be hell to pay from the O5
Council.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:08.149
But somehow, there was no sign of Dee anywhere
in the facility.

00:10:08.149 --> 00:10:12.529
They had gone, scans of the building revealed
that all members of personnel, all anomalies

00:10:12.529 --> 00:10:15.490
and other registered forms of life were all
accounted for.

00:10:15.490 --> 00:10:19.649
It was only when Kylan ran through the mess
hall that they realized where their refined

00:10:19.649 --> 00:10:21.560
test subject had got to.

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:22.790
“Hey, turn that up!”

00:10:22.790 --> 00:10:26.930
they yelled to a security officer who had
been quietly enjoying his lunch break.

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:31.079
Standing on a chair, he reached up and raised
the volume of a TV that was mounted to the

00:10:31.079 --> 00:10:32.910
wall, overlooking the mess hall.

00:10:32.910 --> 00:10:37.040
The screen was depicting a live news report,
the anchor on the ground standing outside

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:39.680
the entrance to an ordinary Ikea store.

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:44.329
“I’m standing outside the very store where
this bizarre turn of events has taken place,”

00:10:44.329 --> 00:10:45.500
the anchor explained.

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:49.300
“Police received numerous calls regarding
sightings of an unknown figure said to be

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:50.300
scaring shoppers.

00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:54.579
However, they only responded when this clip
went viral on social media.”

00:10:54.579 --> 00:10:59.350
The report cut to cell phone footage of none
other than Dee, inside the store.

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:04.320
Their uniform had shifted into its typical
Ikea colors, almost like it had adapted to

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:07.820
suit the place it had somehow transported
itself to.

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:11.500
From the mess hall, Kylan watched the footage
in a mix of shock and confusion.

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:15.960
“Naturally, the reaction from bystanders
was one of fright at the individual’s rather

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:17.810
odd, faceless appearance.

00:11:17.810 --> 00:11:22.050
Some took to Twitter, posting images calling
it some form of viral marketing hoax.

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:26.380
Others claimed it was a publicity stunt by
Ikea to boost sales, although, in a statement,

00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:28.500
the company denies these accusations.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:31.589
However, it was then reported that the supposed
creature began…

00:11:31.589 --> 00:11:35.450
I’m reading this right, aren’t I?” the
anchor paused for a moment.

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:39.769
“Started helping customers by directing
them to store departments, recommending different

00:11:39.769 --> 00:11:45.180
Ikea furniture and, perhaps strangest of all,
did all of this via… oh come on, really?

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:47.389
Telepathic communication.”

00:11:47.389 --> 00:11:50.920
Conley had appeared in the mess hall just
in time to witness the news.

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:55.040
Dee had gotten free and immediately sought
out the nearest Ikea… to work there?

00:11:55.040 --> 00:12:01.200
The next few hours contained a maddening slew
of new information bombarding the Foundation

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:05.769
as Researchers Kylan and Conley scrabbled
to figure out some way of recapturing Dee.

00:12:05.769 --> 00:12:12.300
It didn’t seem that the SCP-3008-2 instance
was a danger to civilians, in fact most reports

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:14.800
stated that they were rather friendly.

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:18.889
Any customers that interacted with the creature
described its new communication patterns in

00:12:18.889 --> 00:12:22.760
five-star reviews they apparently felt compelled
to start posting online.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:25.800
“I’ve never experienced anything like
it,” one wrote.

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:29.699
“Dee offered the most delightful customer
service I have ever received.

00:12:29.699 --> 00:12:32.649
That must be where they got their name, Dee
for delightful!”

00:12:32.649 --> 00:12:36.579
“It’s not like Dee speaks in your head,”
another review explained.

00:12:36.579 --> 00:12:39.949
“It’s more like they just give you their
thoughts, beamed directly in there.

00:12:39.949 --> 00:12:43.890
I said ‘where can I find the Bathrooms and
Fittings department, and instantly Dee had

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:47.240
given me the directions, it was as if I’d
always known!”

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:52.050
Having an anomaly like Dee out in the open
raised all sorts of problems for the Foundation.

00:12:52.050 --> 00:12:55.810
For one, they would have to not only scrub
every mention of the Staff member from the

00:12:55.810 --> 00:13:00.760
internet, but also track down anyone that
interacted with Dee to administer amnestics.

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:05.360
But that was far from the worst of it; the
researchers had been so caught up in coordinating

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:09.970
a recapture effort that they didn’t realize
how rapid and extremely widespread the Dee

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:11.639
reviews were getting.

00:13:11.639 --> 00:13:15.950
They were being left on customer satisfaction
boards for stores in different States, within

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:16.950
minutes of each other.

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:20.890
It took only fifteen minutes for a review
that mentioned Dee to be left in a store that

00:13:20.890 --> 00:13:24.450
wasn’t even an Ikea outlet, but convenience
store.

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:28.520
“Thank you, Dee, for such lovely and speedy
service at the cashier’s desk, never had

00:13:28.520 --> 00:13:32.820
such a nice conversation/interaction with
anyone else in the store before,” the review

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:33.820
read.

00:13:33.820 --> 00:13:38.149
The news that Dee could seemingly be in multiple
places at once, appearing in different stores,

00:13:38.149 --> 00:13:42.949
was confirmed when Conley and Kylan saw photos
posted online of the creature wearing what

00:13:42.949 --> 00:13:45.820
looked like a number of alternate uniforms.

00:13:45.820 --> 00:13:50.920
It seemed that Dee’s clothing – once exclusively
just an Ikea shirt and pants – switched

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:54.380
to match the uniform of whichever store they
starting to work in.

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:58.350
And the more they worked, the more places
they seemed to appear.

00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:02.330
Perhaps the most shocking development came
almost fifty minutes after Dee had been refined

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:03.910
and had disappeared.

00:14:03.910 --> 00:14:08.089
Once again turning their attention to the
news, Researcher Kylan watched as the manager

00:14:08.089 --> 00:14:12.759
of a huge supermarket franchise store appeared
giving an interview live, talking about how

00:14:12.759 --> 00:14:17.450
the altered SCP-3008 Staff had caused him
to change his entire business practice.

00:14:17.450 --> 00:14:19.050
“Listen, Dee is great.

00:14:19.050 --> 00:14:23.029
Our customers love Dee, I hear the company’s
shareholders love ‘em too.

00:14:23.029 --> 00:14:26.949
One thing’s clear we all love Dee!” he
said jovially, but something was unnerving

00:14:26.949 --> 00:14:28.290
about his gleeful smile.

00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:32.170
“So, to show them our appreciation, I am
hereby announcing that – effective immediately

00:14:32.170 --> 00:14:35.740
– all my retail staff are no longer required
to come into work.

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:38.200
Dee does it all, so there’s no need for
anyone else!

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:42.190
They’re friendlier, quieter, they work faster,
and they’re more efficient than any employee

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:43.190
on my payroll!

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:45.430
That’s right folks, Dee’s here to stay.”

00:14:45.430 --> 00:14:50.070
Naturally, this move sparked serious controversy,
with the store’s disgruntled now-former

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:51.450
employees finding themselves out of work.

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:55.699
A number of them took to social media in an
outcry of dissatisfaction.

00:14:55.699 --> 00:14:56.810
“This isn’t fair!

00:14:56.810 --> 00:15:00.370
I’ve worked every weekend through college
at that store, and now I’m fired just like

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:01.370
that?

00:15:01.370 --> 00:15:03.279
Thanks a lot, Dee!” one of them protested.

00:15:03.279 --> 00:15:05.829
“It’s all a corporate ploy,” another
wrote.

00:15:05.829 --> 00:15:09.060
“The rumor is, the only reason they’re
laying us all off so quick is because Dee

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:12.639
doesn’t technically count as a human employee
so they don’t have to pay them.

00:15:12.639 --> 00:15:16.380
They’re working for free so the store manager,
and the company that owns the store, can keep

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:18.130
every penny of the profits.”

00:15:18.130 --> 00:15:22.470
The justified outrage seemed to go wilfully
ignored as another store announced it would

00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:27.800
be adopting the same policy, firing all its
staff and letting Dee take over their duties.

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:31.810
More and more photos started pouring in right
before Conley and Kylan’s eyes of multiple

00:15:31.810 --> 00:15:38.339
refined SCP-3008-2 instances working behind
cashier’s desks, refilling shelves with

00:15:38.339 --> 00:15:40.589
products, assisting customers.

00:15:40.589 --> 00:15:46.569
Dee seemed to be acting out of instinct, like
they couldn’t help being Staff; it was their

00:15:46.569 --> 00:15:47.569
purpose.

00:15:47.569 --> 00:15:51.670
The horde of anomalous Staff members ended
up swarming over the country’s retail industry

00:15:51.670 --> 00:15:54.870
simultaneously, like the drones of an ant
colony.

00:15:54.870 --> 00:15:57.140
“Kylan, what the hell have we done?”

00:15:57.140 --> 00:15:59.760
Conley asked, staring in disbelief at the
TV screen.

00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:03.620
“We’ve done the unthinkable,” they answered,
equally horrified.

00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:05.170
“We created a monster.

00:16:05.170 --> 00:16:09.330
We took Dee out of SCP-3008 and made them
into the most powerful retail worker on the

00:16:09.330 --> 00:16:10.330
planet.”

00:16:10.330 --> 00:16:15.000
Within hours, every retail outlet of every
different description – not just Ikea – had

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:19.720
reported the firing of their entire staff,
and every business that did was now raking

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:21.500
in record profits.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:26.380
Droves of shoppers flocked to stores, all
enjoying Dee’s customer service so much

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:29.810
that they were taking any excuse they could
to rush out and buy…

00:16:29.810 --> 00:16:31.269
well, anything.

00:16:31.269 --> 00:16:36.350
As stock supplies started to deplete, more
and more instances of the altered SCP-3008-2

00:16:36.350 --> 00:16:41.069
appeared, taking over the supply chain and
distributing products to the various stores

00:16:41.069 --> 00:16:44.500
they were working at, refilling the shelves
in record time.

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:47.910
Naturally, the O5 Council were furious.

00:16:47.910 --> 00:16:52.680
Researchers Kylan and Conley had hoped to
present them with a refined SCP-3008 Staff

00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:56.170
member that could allow them to better understand
the Infinite Ikea.

00:16:56.170 --> 00:17:00.721
Now, the Council’s ulterior motive of having
access to an interdimensional bridge to other

00:17:00.721 --> 00:17:02.870
universes had been dashed.

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:07.339
As if that wasn’t bad enough, and the added
hassle of Dee rapidly becoming a worldwide

00:17:07.339 --> 00:17:10.709
sensation, the economy was destabilizing.

00:17:10.709 --> 00:17:14.480
Thanks to the retail companies firing their
staff and hoarding massive amounts of profit

00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:20.870
from all their stores, thanks to having Dee
compulsively working there, refining an SCP-3008

00:17:20.870 --> 00:17:25.120
Staff member looked like it was about to collapse
the stock market and plunge the whole world

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:26.640
into chaos.

00:17:26.640 --> 00:17:29.350
“Um, our bad?”

00:17:29.350 --> 00:17:33.620
Researcher Kylan shrugged, unsure what to
say after they and Conley had just been brought

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:36.840
before the shadowy O5 Council to be reprimanded.

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:42.010
There was only one thing for it: Dee had to
be taken out of the picture, and quickly.

00:17:42.010 --> 00:17:45.900
The more they worked, the more they seemed
to be able to multiply and spread.

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:50.700
Then, with a greater number of Dee instances
within a store, the faster and more efficient

00:17:50.700 --> 00:17:52.000
they were able to work.

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:57.669
So, in retaliation, the O5 Council begrudgingly
activated Mobile Task Force Alpha-1, better

00:17:57.669 --> 00:18:00.549
known by their codename, Red Right Hand.

00:18:00.549 --> 00:18:04.660
This task force reported directly to the Council,
they were some of the Foundation’s most

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:08.770
loyal operatives, and it was far from their
first assassination mission.

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:14.090
Well, they had assumed it would be an assassination,
dispatching the Red Right Hand to the nearby

00:18:14.090 --> 00:18:18.390
Ikea where Dee had first transported themselves
to after exiting SCP-914.

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:21.430
Of course, the place was overrun with Dee
duplicates.

00:18:21.430 --> 00:18:25.630
But even after clearing out the entire store
and administering amnestics to any customers

00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:29.500
that witnessed it, there were still plenty
more of Dee out there.

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:33.280
The Council quickly realized that they’d
have to send MTF Alpha-1 to every branch of

00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:38.730
every outlet in the country, systematically
taking out every duplicate of Dee in a lengthy

00:18:38.730 --> 00:18:41.880
clean-up operation until they were no more.

00:18:41.880 --> 00:18:45.850
It seemed the Foundation’s personnel had
their work cut out for them; hopefully they’d

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:51.000
be entitled to a raise and some paid time
off after this was all over.

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:56.870
Now go check out “How To Actually Beat SCP-3008
The Infinite Ikea” and “I Survived 100

00:18:56.870 --> 00:18:58.620
Days in SCP-3008...

00:18:58.620 --> 00:19:00.830
Here's What Happened” for more of the world’s
most Hygge anomaly!

